{"author":{"id":"2f242a7e7f2592f8909954a77fabece74f6e8cc197182647ed3b15ea8e3878af"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791750098,"nonce":"MXMhlKjeYY/AtIzjEX3G8DvzQY4=","title":"Expose gamepads through the shared API and browser IDL","message":"ChimpMonk input issue 5486670 needs native gamepads. The user chose xwindow as their home and explicitly requested supporting IDL. hlwindow is the HashLink/Ash adapter for xwindow, whose native window backend uses winit; all runtime surfaces must be generated from the same declaration.\n\nAdd named standard-layout buttons, four stick axes and analog triggers; enumeration, connection-scoped handles, hot-plug events, current state and capability reporting; finite-duration dual-motor rumble where supported. Use a runtime-neutral shared state model, a desktop gilrs backend, and browser Gamepad API sampling. Declare the Haxe API in api/window.api.rs, vendor the corresponding browser Gamepad WebIDL beside the existing specification snapshot, and extend the page agent's IDL commands/events. Preserve existing window event indices and ABI. Gamepad events have one application-wide queue, independent of per-window keyboard/pointer queues; waking an idle native window must not require periodic main-thread polling.\n\nGenerate all runtime APIs, and update hlwindow's consuming dependency and generated surface from the same revision. Verify independent canonical button/axis normalization, connect/disconnect/stale handles, event ordering and current state, browser agent-\u003ewire round trips and rumble parameters, generated models for Caribou/HashLink/Rayzor, native and threaded-wasm compilation, and an Ash/Haxe smoke test. Hardware verification depends on an attached controller and must be reported separately from injected backend checks. Add a runnable API example and document platform capabilities explicitly; don't claim unsupported mobile or rumble backends.\n\nUse sequential resource-guarded builds with one Cargo worker after the host OOM. Keep changes local, use full git-bug trailers on commits, and do not push.","files":null}]}